Request Time: 0 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"174.104.232.82","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":80226,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"46d939cbc68652e255d2ad63fb7a9bf6","RawContent":"@[member=\"MesaMiso\"] Congratulations to you too! I commented some to you on another thread about my wedding planner anxiety. \ud83d\ude10 The other planning stuff is going well. We sent out invitations in November with a deposit due date of March 3. Planning on sending a post card to those who have made comments but haven&#039;t RSVP&#039;d or made a deposit a couple weeks prior to that. I will not harass some family members who we *had* to invite, but knew they wouldn&#039;t\/couldn&#039;t come. Hahahahaha\n\n\nWe are doing a dia de los muertos theme and people really loved the invites! We&#039;re doing teal and orange, not gothic or Halloween looking. We&#039;re only having a maid of honor and best man. Our dresses are bought, the guys will be figured out this summer. I bought oot bags from wedding chicks on black Friday for 50% off. We&#039;re expecting a small group, so I just got 24. Planning on tumblers, key card holders, hangover kits etc. But I&#039;m waiting until we have a definite number. Then Etsy will be in the cards constantly, because I am not a crafter. I used a hand stamp on the back of the invites and that was stressful. Hahah Also ordering flowers from Etsy, I love sola flowers, so I hope they make it there in 1 piece! I found metal buckets at Target at Halloween with a cut out sugar skull and a papal picado type border. I&#039;m going to spray paint them and use them for centerpieces with flowers and tea lights. Also getting mini sugar skull pinatas for the table and doing custom maracas for favors. \n\n\nWe used Beach Bum Vacations for our room block. Lisa is great. She&#039;s been able to communicate with them better than me. I&#039;m going to be patient until I have a number, and then be more aggressive in getting everything in writing to change our reception. \n\n\nHow&#039;s your planning going? How many people are you expecting?\n\n\n\n\nSent from my Pixel XL using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1917168,"PostDate":1485957274,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"288342\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='https:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/288342-mesamiso\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">MesaMiso<\/span><\/a> Congratulations to you too! I commented some to you on another thread about my wedding planner anxiety. \ud83d\ude10 The other planning stuff is going well. We sent out invitations in November with a deposit due date of March 3. Planning on sending a post card to those who have made comments but haven't RSVP'd or made a deposit a couple weeks prior to that. I will not harass some family members who we *had* to invite, but knew they wouldn't\/couldn't come. Hahahahaha<br><br>\nWe are doing a dia de los muertos theme and people really loved the invites! We're doing teal and orange, not gothic or Halloween looking. We're only having a maid of honor and best man. Our dresses are bought, the guys will be figured out this summer. I bought oot bags from wedding chicks on black Friday for 50% off. We're expecting a small group, so I just got 24. Planning on tumblers, key card holders, hangover kits etc. But I'm waiting until we have a definite number. Then Etsy will be in the cards constantly, because I am not a crafter. I used a hand stamp on the back of the invites and that was stressful. Hahah Also ordering flowers from Etsy, I love sola flowers, so I hope they make it there in 1 piece! I found metal buckets at Target at Halloween with a cut out sugar skull and a papal picado type border. I'm going to spray paint them and use them for centerpieces with flowers and tea lights. Also getting mini sugar skull pinatas for the table and doing custom maracas for favors. <br><br>\nWe used Beach Bum Vacations for our room block. Lisa is great. She's been able to communicate with them better than me. I'm going to be patient until I have a number, and then be more aggressive in getting everything in writing to change our reception. <br><br>\nHow's your planning going? How many people are you expecting?<br><br><br><br>\nSent from my Pixel XL using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"rebeccarpeck@gmail.com","IpAddress":"174.104.232.82","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1472782482,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"https:\/\/bdw-stevewright.netdna-ssl.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"rebeccarpeck1","Id":287671,"Name":"rebeccarpeck1","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"76.220.0.70","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":80226,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"9f095ed0374c12019403da801a60c19a","RawContent":"[quote name=\"rebeccarpeck1\" post=\"1917168\" timestamp=\"1485957274\"]\n@[member=\"MesaMiso\"] Congratulations to you too! I commented some to you on another thread about my wedding planner anxiety.  The other planning stuff is going well. We sent out invitations in November with a deposit due date of March 3. Planning on sending a post card to those who have made comments but haven&#039;t RSVP&#039;d or made a deposit a couple weeks prior to that. I will not harass some family members who we *had* to invite, but knew they wouldn&#039;t\/couldn&#039;t come. Hahahahaha\n\nWe are doing a dia de los muertos theme and people really loved the invites! We&#039;re doing teal and orange, not gothic or Halloween looking. We&#039;re only having a maid of honor and best man. Our dresses are bought, the guys will be figured out this summer. I bought oot bags from wedding chicks on black Friday for 50% off. We&#039;re expecting a small group, so I just got 24. Planning on tumblers, key card holders, hangover kits etc. But I&#039;m waiting until we have a definite number. Then Etsy will be in the cards constantly, because I am not a crafter. I used a hand stamp on the back of the invites and that was stressful. Hahah Also ordering flowers from Etsy, I love sola flowers, so I hope they make it there in 1 piece! I found metal buckets at Target at Halloween with a cut out sugar skull and a papal picado type border. I&#039;m going to spray paint them and use them for centerpieces with flowers and tea lights. Also getting mini sugar skull pinatas for the table and doing custom maracas for favors.\n\nWe used Beach Bum Vacations for our room block. Lisa is great. She&#039;s been able to communicate with them better than me. I&#039;m going to be patient until I have a number, and then be more aggressive in getting everything in writing to change our reception.\n\nHow&#039;s your planning going? How many people are you expecting?\n\n\n\nSent from my Pixel XL using Tapatalk[\/quote]@[member=\"rebeccarpeck1\"] WOW! You are sooo on top of it!! I literally haven&#039;t done anything yet :\/  Everything you&#039;re doing sounds amazing!! I would love to start sending out my save the dates but I just don&#039;t know how to direct my guest with booking. Did you hire your travel agent on your own or did Hyatt Ziva assign one? We are expecting to have about 50-60 but who knows since it is a destination wedding. Did you do the big day preview? Did you book your vendors already?","Attachments":[],"Id":1917178,"PostDate":1486039884,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>rebeccarpeck1, on 01 February 2017 - 05:54 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"288342\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='https:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/288342-mesamiso\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">MesaMiso<\/span><\/a> Congratulations to you too! I commented some to you on another thread about my wedding planner anxiety.  The other planning stuff is going well. We sent out invitations in November with a deposit due date of March 3. Planning on sending a post card to those who have made comments but haven't RSVP'd or made a deposit a couple weeks prior to that. I will not harass some family members who we *had* to invite, but knew they wouldn't\/couldn't come. Hahahahaha<br><br>\nWe are doing a dia de los muertos theme and people really loved the invites! We're doing teal and orange, not gothic or Halloween looking. We're only having a maid of honor and best man. Our dresses are bought, the guys will be figured out this summer. I bought oot bags from wedding chicks on black Friday for 50% off. We're expecting a small group, so I just got 24. Planning on tumblers, key card holders, hangover kits etc. But I'm waiting until we have a definite number. Then Etsy will be in the cards constantly, because I am not a crafter. I used a hand stamp on the back of the invites and that was stressful. Hahah Also ordering flowers from Etsy, I love sola flowers, so I hope they make it there in 1 piece! I found metal buckets at Target at Halloween with a cut out sugar skull and a papal picado type border. I'm going to spray paint them and use them for centerpieces with flowers and tea lights. Also getting mini sugar skull pinatas for the table and doing custom maracas for favors.<br><br>\nWe used Beach Bum Vacations for our room block. Lisa is great. She's been able to communicate with them better than me. I'm going to be patient until I have a number, and then be more aggressive in getting everything in writing to change our reception.<br><br>\nHow's your planning going? How many people are you expecting?<br><br><br><br>\nSent from my Pixel XL using Tapatalk<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"287671\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='https:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/287671-rebeccarpeck1\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">rebeccarpeck1<\/span><\/a> WOW! You are sooo on top of it!! I literally haven't done anything yet :\/ \u00a0Everything you're doing sounds amazing!! I would love to start sending out my save the dates but I just don't know how to direct my guest with booking. Did you hire your travel agent on your own or did Hyatt Ziva assign one? We are expecting to have about 50-60 but who knows since it is a destination wedding. Did you do the big day preview? Did you book your vendors already?<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"mesalukman@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"99.127.4.233","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1484960407,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"https:\/\/bdw-stevewright.netdna-ssl.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"MesaMiso","Id":288342,"Name":"MesaMiso","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"174.104.232.82","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":80226,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"42c6fa83f59e980f2dde7ae0f2a3f4fb","RawContent":"@[member=\"MesaMiso\"] Don&#039;t worry, you have plenty of time and it will all come together! We had originally talked about getting Married in November 2016, but it didn&#039;t pan out for a few reasons, so I have been searching for things for a long time!\n\n\nWe got 3 quotes on rooms, 2 online and one from a local travel agency. We chose Beach Bum because not only was it the least expensive, but I really felt a good connection with my agent, Lisa. I just felt like people depending on us (me hahahahaha) for travel arrangements would just be something I didn&#039;t want to deal with. Now, she can arrange flights, but we and many of our guests will book our own flights with miles\/points.\n\n\nA travel agent can also help communicate with the wedding department. This has been invaluable since we are on the 6th planner! Lisa got me emails within a day, after I had waited up to 2 weeks. Things are better now, so maybe the changes they made at the end of last year are getting the bugs out. \n\n\nWe aren&#039;t able to do a preview, so that kind of adds to the amount of questions I have. We aren&#039;t having a DJ , it&#039;s just not \"us.\" One of the reasons we chose a destination wedding is to avoid many of the expected or traditional wedding things! We&#039;re using the resort&#039;s vendor for lighting (we&#039;re having the reception by the fire pits), I&#039;m bringing decor, so that&#039;s not an issue. The place where we are still undecided is photography. Photopro \"seems\" OK, but we&#039;re still thinking we might splurge and get an outside vendor. \n\n\nHave you made any progress? \n\n\nSent from my Pixel XL using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1917223,"PostDate":1486734893,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"288342\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='https:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/288342-mesamiso\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">MesaMiso<\/span><\/a> Don't worry, you have plenty of time and it will all come together! We had originally talked about getting Married in November 2016, but it didn't pan out for a few reasons, so I have been searching for things for a long time!<br><br>\nWe got 3 quotes on rooms, 2 online and one from a local travel agency. We chose Beach Bum because not only was it the least expensive, but I really felt a good connection with my agent, Lisa. I just felt like people depending on us (me hahahahaha) for travel arrangements would just be something I didn't want to deal with. Now, she can arrange flights, but we and many of our guests will book our own flights with miles\/points.<br><br>\nA travel agent can also help communicate with the wedding department. This has been invaluable since we are on the 6th planner! Lisa got me emails within a day, after I had waited up to 2 weeks. Things are better now, so maybe the changes they made at the end of last year are getting the bugs out. <br><br>\nWe aren't able to do a preview, so that kind of adds to the amount of questions I have. We aren't having a DJ , it's just not \"us.\" One of the reasons we chose a destination wedding is to avoid many of the expected or traditional wedding things! We're using the resort's vendor for lighting (we're having the reception by the fire pits), I'm bringing decor, so that's not an issue. The place where we are still undecided is photography. Photopro \"seems\" OK, but we're still thinking we might splurge and get an outside vendor. <br><br>\nHave you made any progress? <br><br>\nSent from my Pixel XL using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"rebeccarpeck@gmail.com","IpAddress":"174.104.232.82","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1472782482,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"https:\/\/bdw-stevewright.netdna-ssl.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"rebeccarpeck1","Id":287671,"Name":"rebeccarpeck1","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"99.127.4.233","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":80226,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"35e74380e4eb1bd7b8ae15c28e287792","RawContent":"[quote name=\"rebeccarpeck1\" post=\"1917223\" timestamp=\"1486734893\"]\n@[member=\"MesaMiso\"] Don&#039;t worry, you have plenty of time and it will all come together! We had originally talked about getting Married in November 2016, but it didn&#039;t pan out for a few reasons, so I have been searching for things for a long time!\n\nWe got 3 quotes on rooms, 2 online and one from a local travel agency. We chose Beach Bum because not only was it the least expensive, but I really felt a good connection with my agent, Lisa. I just felt like people depending on us (me hahahahaha) for travel arrangements would just be something I didn&#039;t want to deal with. Now, she can arrange flights, but we and many of our guests will book our own flights with miles\/points.\n\nA travel agent can also help communicate with the wedding department. This has been invaluable since we are on the 6th planner! Lisa got me emails within a day, after I had waited up to 2 weeks. Things are better now, so maybe the changes they made at the end of last year are getting the bugs out.\n\nWe aren&#039;t able to do a preview, so that kind of adds to the amount of questions I have. We aren&#039;t having a DJ , it&#039;s just not \"us.\" One of the reasons we chose a destination wedding is to avoid many of the expected or traditional wedding things! We&#039;re using the resort&#039;s vendor for lighting (we&#039;re having the reception by the fire pits), I&#039;m bringing decor, so that&#039;s not an issue. The place where we are still undecided is photography. Photopro \"seems\" OK, but we&#039;re still thinking we might splurge and get an outside vendor.\n\nHave you made any progress?\n\nSent from my Pixel XL using Tapatalk[\/quote]@[member=\"rebeccarpeck1\"] I totally agree with you regarding Photopro. Do you know how much it is for outside vendors? Do you need to get them a guest pass on top of paying the outside vendor fees? Sounds like you have a great travel agent!! Will your travel agent match prices if one of your guest find a cheaper price on another website like expedia? I&#039;m still debating on booking a travel agent. \n\nHow is everything going with you? Hope all is well!! Happy Valentines day!!","Attachments":[],"Id":1917244,"PostDate":1487116925,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>rebeccarpeck1, on 10 February 2017 - 05:54 AM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"288342\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='https:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/288342-mesamiso\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">MesaMiso<\/span><\/a> Don't worry, you have plenty of time and it will all come together! We had originally talked about getting Married in November 2016, but it didn't pan out for a few reasons, so I have been searching for things for a long time!<br><br>\nWe got 3 quotes on rooms, 2 online and one from a local travel agency. We chose Beach Bum because not only was it the least expensive, but I really felt a good connection with my agent, Lisa. I just felt like people depending on us (me hahahahaha) for travel arrangements would just be something I didn't want to deal with. Now, she can arrange flights, but we and many of our guests will book our own flights with miles\/points.<br><br>\nA travel agent can also help communicate with the wedding department. This has been invaluable since we are on the 6th planner! Lisa got me emails within a day, after I had waited up to 2 weeks. Things are better now, so maybe the changes they made at the end of last year are getting the bugs out.<br><br>\nWe aren't able to do a preview, so that kind of adds to the amount of questions I have. We aren't having a DJ , it's just not \"us.\" One of the reasons we chose a destination wedding is to avoid many of the expected or traditional wedding things! We're using the resort's vendor for lighting (we're having the reception by the fire pits), I'm bringing decor, so that's not an issue. The place where we are still undecided is photography. Photopro \"seems\" OK, but we're still thinking we might splurge and get an outside vendor.<br><br>\nHave you made any progress?<br><br>\nSent from my Pixel XL using Tapatalk<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"287671\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='https:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/287671-rebeccarpeck1\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">rebeccarpeck1<\/span><\/a> I totally agree with you regarding Photopro. Do you know how much it is for outside vendors? Do you need to get them a guest pass on top of paying the outside vendor fees? Sounds like you have a great travel agent!! Will your travel agent match prices if one of your guest find a cheaper price on another website like expedia? I'm still debating on booking a travel agent.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>How is everything going with you? Hope all is well!! Happy Valentines day!!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"mesalukman@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"99.127.4.233","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1484960407,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"https:\/\/bdw-stevewright.netdna-ssl.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"MesaMiso","Id":288342,"Name":"MesaMiso","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":14,"TotalPages":2,"CurrentPage":10,"NextPage":-1,"PreviousPage":0,"LastPage":10},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":1,"Type":"int"}]}
